      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Compound of {駆|く} ('to drive; to gallop') and {動|どう} ('to move'). Originally described driving horses at speed, now almost exclusively used in mechanical and technological contexts.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {四輪|よんりん}{駆動|くどう} (4WD): four-wheel drive\n- {前輪|ぜんりん}{駆動|くどう} (FWD): front-wheel drive\n- {後輪|こうりん}{駆動|くどう} (RWD): rear-wheel drive\n- {駆動|くどう}{方式|ほうしき}: drive system; drive type\n- {駆動|くどう}{力|りょく}: driving force; motive power\n- {電気|でんき}{駆動|くどう}: electric drive\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {動力|どうりょく}: motive power; power source — emphasizes the energy source rather than the transmission mechanism\n- {推進|すいしん}: propulsion; promotion — used for rockets, ships, and figuratively for driving initiatives forward\n- {運転|うんてん}: operation; driving — focuses on the human act of operating a vehicle or machine",
